{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385404-how-do-you-handle-post-cognition-time-2-plus-additional-spheres","id":1385404,"title":"How do you handle Post-cognition (Time 2 plus additional spheres)?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-03T07:58:43-07:00","id":1385404,"title":"How do you handle Post-cognition (Time 2 plus additional spheres)?","content":"Hi. <br /> <br /> Well...that. How do you do it, specially over objects (Matter)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T08:11:52-07:00","id":1385405,"title":"","content":"I like to narrate from the perspective of the object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T08:31:18-07:00","id":1385410,"title":"","content":"As stated above, from the perspective of the object, which I feel is critical. Additionally, unless its for something quick and not going to give away something of story breaking importance, the &quot;vision&quot; should be entirely symbolic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T10:26:13-07:00","id":1385428,"title":"","content":"Can you guys tell me more about it (perspective of the object), please? I ask because, since objects have no senses, I wouldnt know how to portray that. It's easier to say &quot;you hear, you see, you feel&quot;...but an object cant see or hear or feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T11:25:18-07:00","id":1385433,"title":"","content":"In my games I generally allow that an object can perceive its immediate surroundings. I wouldnt give more than 10 feet away normally. The object would know if it was interacted with or moved. I do not allow objects to differentiate between people, though it might determine a gentle grasp from a harsh or forced one. <br /> <br /> I allow objects to know how they were used, i.e. if they were thrown, fired ( in the case of a gun) and whatnot. If the object were a computer it would know it was used to type a letter, and which keys, and in what order, they were used thereby having the ability to know what was typed.<br /> <br /> In my opinion it is much better to use Pre and Post Cognitive effects on areas rather than on objects. Unless of course your interest is in where the object has been.<br /> <br /> Many times it is more beneficial to examine the psychic resonance of an object for residual impressions left by their last user","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 05-03-2020, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T22:42:00-07:00","id":1385543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385404-how-do-you-handle-post-cognition-time-2-plus-additional-spheres?p=1385433#post1385433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games I generally allow that an object can perceive its immediate surroundings. I wouldnt give more than 10 feet away normally. The object would know if it was interacted with or moved. I do not allow objects to differentiate between people, though it might determine a gentle grasp from a harsh or forced one.<br /> <br /> I allow objects to know how they were used, i.e. if they were thrown, fired ( in the case of a gun) and whatnot. If the object were a computer it would know it was used to type a letter, and which keys, and in what order, they were used thereby having the ability to know what was typed.<br /> <br /> In my opinion it is much better to use Pre and Post Cognitive effects on areas rather than on objects. Unless of course your interest is in where the object has been.<br /> <br /> Many times it is more beneficial to examine the psychic resonance of an object for residual impressions left by their last user</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The character doesnt have access to the location, just the object, which can be associated to a particular event.<br /> <br /> How do you describe that psychic resonance? Thats something I have never understood completely in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T06:33:47-07:00","id":1385599,"title":"","content":"Reaonace is described a bit in M20 and extensively in Book of Secrets. In simple terms Resonance is psychic emotion descriptor that is carried by all things. People, objects, places and Magick. Its what gets left behind as psychic residue. The more powerful the emotion the more powerful the lingering resonance will be.<br /> <br /> When something is examined with Mind 1 or Prime 1 for psychic or magical traces it is this resonance that is being read. It is the psychic or magick fingerprints that are left behind. For Magick it is a way tp identify the caster of an effect if you can get a clear enough &quot;fingerprint&quot; of an effect and match it to the Resonance Aura of the caster. <br /> <br /> It can also be used to tell the state of mind in which a Mage works their magick. Are they gentle, meticulous, enraged, etc. The same goes for the user of an object with psychic resonance.<br /> <br /> Resonance can also be tricky so you don't want to jump to conclusions. A scalpel could read with a resonance of calm and precision. Does that mean it was used in surgery, or by Jack the Ripper. Obviously the more success one obtains in reading an objects resonance the more emotions and their intensity can be determined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}